00:01:25.000 --> 00:02:14.000
episode on your app or on our website. The night of Friday, December 20, 1968, two years after the murder of Sherry Joe Bates in Benesha, California. It was between 9.30 and 10 o'clock when a small sports car slowly came to a stop on a gravel turnout, half a mile down the road from Lake Herman. Behind the wheel was William Crow. The car belonged to his girlfriend who was riding beside him in the passenger seat. Although the car was new, it was having some troubles, so William had taken it for a cruise
节目简介。1968年12月20日星期五晚，即加利福尼亚州贝尼西亚的谢莉·乔·贝茨谋杀案发生两年后。时间在9点30分到10点之间，一辆小型跑车缓缓停在距离赫尔曼湖半英里远的公路旁砾石岔道上。方向盘后坐着威廉·克劳。这辆车属于他的女友，她正坐在他身旁的副驾驶座上。虽然这辆车是新的，但有些小毛病，所以威廉开车兜风

4
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:55.000
to test out the engine. His route led him down Lake Herman Road, a five-mile stretch that curved through the countryside to the neighbouring city of Vallejo. Traffic along Lake Herman Road was sparse during the day and near non-existent at night. It was a lonely, quiet road framed by fields, trees and ranches that stretched over the rolling hills. With no street lights to illuminate the scenery, the area had become a lover's lane of sorts. Living couples seeking privacy would park their cars in the numerous turnouts that lined
来测试发动机。他的路线沿着赫尔曼湖路前行，这是一段长达五英里的路段，在乡村蜿蜒穿过，通往邻近的瓦列霍市。白天，赫尔曼湖路上的车流量稀少，到了晚上几乎空无一人。这是一条荒凉、安静的道路，两旁是被起伏的山丘上绵延的田野、树木和牧场。由于没有路灯照亮风景，这个地区在某种程度上成了约会圣地。寻求隐私的情侣们会把车停在沿路的众多岔道上。

