00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:32.000
the road. William Crow pulled into one such turnout, situated at the gated number 10 entrance to the Benesha water pumping station. He positioned the car so that its rear faced the gate and the headlights illuminated the road. Soon, his attention was drawn to a growing light. Our vehicle was travelling down Lake Herman Road towards Vallejo. It rolled along in the pitch-black darkness until it reached the gate number 10 turnout.
威廉·克劳将车驶入其中一个岔道，该岔道位于贝尼西亚水泵站10号大门旁。他调整了车位，让车尾对着大门，车灯照亮了道路。很快，他的注意力被一束越来越亮的灯光吸引了。一辆汽车正沿着赫尔曼湖路开往瓦列霍方向。它在漆黑的暗夜中行驶，直到开到10号大门的岔道口。

6
00:03:32.000 --> 00:04:09.000
William's headlights swept over the car as it passed and he caught a quick glimpse of the driver. He was male with short hair and glasses. The car itself was a light-coloured four-door Chevrolet Impala, a classic late 1950s model with a hard top and tail fin. The Chevy had barely cleared the turnout when it stopped abruptly in the middle of the road. Its tail lights lit up and it began reversing. Something about this sudden move made William uneasy.
当这辆车驶过时，威廉的车灯扫过了它，他瞥了一眼司机。那是一个留着短发、戴着眼镜的男子。这辆车本身是一辆浅色的四门雪佛兰Impala，是一款经典的1950年代后期车型，带有硬顶和尾鳍。这辆雪佛兰刚驶过岔道就在路中间猛地停了下来。它的尾灯亮起，开始倒车。这种突然的举动让威廉感到有些不安。

7
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:49.000
He immediately felt compelled to leave, so he drove back onto Lake Herman Road and headed in the opposite direction of the Chevy towards Benesha. Keeping an eye on the rearview mirror, William watched the Chevy reverse into the turnout. Within seconds, it turned around, rolled back onto Lake Herman Road and sped up until it was right behind William. The Chevy's driver then started flashing his high beams. William was tempted to pull over and confront the driver, but his terrified girlfriend convinced him not to.
他立刻觉得必须离开，于是把车开回赫尔曼湖路，朝着与雪佛兰相反的方向开往贝尼西亚。威廉盯着后视镜，看着雪佛兰倒车进入岔道。几秒钟之内，它转过身来，重新开上赫尔曼湖路，加速直到紧跟在威廉身后。接着，雪佛兰的司机开始闪烁远光灯。威廉很想把车停路边去和司机理论，但他吓坏了的女友说服了他。

8
00:04:49.000 --> 00:05:26.000
Instead, he sped up to create some distance between the two vehicles. The other driver matched his speed and then some. William glanced back. The Chevy's right front fender was closing in on the sports car's rear quarter panel. Irritation turned to dread as William shifted to a lower gear and slammed the gas pedal to the floor. Up ahead was a fork in the road. The Chevy remained hot on William's tail as he sped towards it.
相反，他加速以拉开两辆车之间的距离。另一位司机匹配了他的速度，甚至更快。威廉往后瞥了一眼。雪佛兰右前翼子板正在逼近跑车的右后侧。随着威廉换入低档并将油门踩到底，烦躁转为了恐惧。前方是一个岔路口。威廉加速朝它驶去时，雪佛兰依然紧咬不放。

9
00:05:26.000 --> 00:06:06.000
Waiting until the very last moment, William gave the steering wheel a sharp turn, sending his car flying down the turnoff. The Chevy, far too heavy to make such a tight turn so quickly, barreled onwards. After traveling 200 yards, William braked to a stop. He turned to look back towards the intersection and was shocked to see the Chevy sitting idle in the middle of Lake Herman Road. Starting with rage, William yelled expletives and threats in the direction of the other driver.
一直等到最后一刻，威廉猛地打方向盘，让他的车飞速驶入岔道。雪佛兰因为太重，无法这么快做出如此急的转弯，因而直冲了过去。行驶了200码后，威廉踩刹车停了下来。他转身向十字路口看去，震惊地发现雪佛兰正空转着停在赫尔曼湖路中间。伴随着愤怒，威廉朝着另一个司机的方向大喊脏话和威胁。

10
00:06:06.000 --> 00:07:15.000
The Chevy waited in the darkness, its engine quietly rumbling in response. After a short wait, the Chevy finally began to move. William watched nervously, his foot resting against the accelerator. The Chevy performed a U-turn and, to William's surprise, drove back towards Vallejo. The chase was over. The impulse to go after the Chevy and face its driver was soon overwhelmed by the instinct to do the exact opposite. Following his guard, William drove home.
雪佛兰在黑暗中等待着，发动机作为回应发出安静的轰鸣声。短暂等待后，雪佛兰终于开始移动。威廉紧张地看着，脚踩在油门上。雪佛兰掉了个头，令威廉吃惊的是，它朝着瓦列霍方向开回去。追逐结束了。想要追上去面对雪佛兰司机的冲动，很快就被做截然相反事情的本能所压倒。遵循直觉，威廉开车回了家。

11
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:55.000
A short while later, a two-toned 1961 AMC Rambler station wagon pulled into the gravel turn out at Gate 10. 17-year-old David Faraday had borrowed the car from his mother so he could take 16-year-old Betty Lou Jensen out for their first date. The pair had recently met while serving on a decorating committee for an upcoming music festival. David was the quintessential good-natured all-American youth who split his spare time between the Eagle Scouts and his high school wrestling team.
不久之后，一辆双色1961年AMC Rambler旅行车开进了10号大门的砾石岔道。17岁的大卫·法拉第向母亲借了这辆车，好带16岁的贝蒂·露·延森去他们的第一次约会。两人最近在为一个即将到来的音乐节的装饰委员会服务时相识。大卫是一个典型的善良、根正苗红的美国青年，他的业余时间分给了鹰级童子军和他的高中摔跤队。

12
00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:34.000
Betty Lou, a popular student at a neighbouring school, was smitten. By December 20, 1968, Betty Lou had only known David for one week, but all signs pointed to him becoming her first boyfriend. At eight o'clock that night, David arrived at the Jensen house to formally meet Betty Lou's parents. After he'd made a good impression, the teens left, with David promising to have Betty Lou home by 11. The teens were cutting it close to curfew when they parked at the turn out at around
贝蒂·露是邻校的一名受欢迎的学生，她已经深深迷恋上了他。到1968年12月20日，贝蒂·露认识大卫才一个星期，但所有迹象都表明他将成为她的第一个男朋友。当晚8点，大卫来到延森家，正式拜访贝蒂·露的父母。在留下好印象后，两个年轻人离开了，大卫答应贝蒂·露在11点前送她回家。当他们在大约10点15分在岔道停车时，

13
00:08:34.000 --> 00:09:11.000
10.15. Clining in their seats, Betty Lou rested her head on David's shoulder and looked out the windshield at the darkened fields to the east. She had never been on a date before, but the fact they'd ended up on Lake Herman Road meant that things were going well. They had the turn out to themselves, with only the occasional car passing by, and the teens soon lost track of time. It was minutes after 11pm when their solitude was disturbed by a bright light.
两个年轻人已经临近宵禁时间。贝蒂·露依偎在座位上，把头靠在大卫的肩膀上，透过挡风玻璃望着东边黑暗的田野。她以前从未约会过，但他们最终来到赫尔曼湖路这一事实意味着一切都很顺利。岔道只有他们自己，偶尔有车驶过，两个年轻人很快就失去了时间的概念。午夜11点过几分，他们的清静被一束强光打破了。

14
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:53.000
It was emanating from a pencil-sized flashlight that was taped to the barrel of a handgun. A male's voice ordered Betty Lou and David to get out. When the teenagers failed to follow his order, he started firing. One bullet ricocheted off the roof above the rambler's back passenger door. Another punctured the left rear wheel well. The third pierced the right rear window, causing the glass to crack. These were just warning shots. Now Betty Lou and David did as they were told.
它散发自一支用胶带缠在手枪枪管上的铅笔大小的手电筒。一个男人的声音命令贝蒂·露和大卫下车。当这两个年轻人没有听从他的命令时，他开始开枪。一颗子弹从Rambler后乘客车门上方的车顶反弹开来。另一颗子弹击穿了左后轮拱。第三颗子弹穿透了右后车窗，导致玻璃碎裂。这些只是警告射击。现在贝蒂·露和大卫照做了。

15
00:09:53.000 --> 00:10:31.000
A frightened Betty Lou unlocked her door and stepped into the cold night. David followed closely behind, scrambling over the bench seat from the driver's side. He had barely lifted himself out when the gun was pressed to his head and its trigger was pulled. David tumbled from the car and fell on his back by the rambler's rear wheel. Betty Lou sprinted towards the road. The shooter raised his weapon and fired off six quick shots. One bullet flew right by her.
受惊的贝蒂·露解开她的车门，踏入寒冷的夜晚。大卫紧随其后，从驾驶座那边翻过长凳座椅。他刚把自己拉起来，手枪就抵住了他的头并扣动了扳机。大卫从车里跌落下来，仰面倒在Rambler的后轮旁。贝蒂·露朝公路冲去。凶手举起武器，连续开了六枪。一颗子弹从她身旁飞过。

16
00:10:31.000 --> 00:11:14.000
The rest burrowed into the right side of her back, causing her to collapse onto her side a few strides shy of the road. With both teams down, the attacker fled. He didn't pass Stella Borges, who was driving along Lake Herman Road to pick her son up from a movie theater in Benesha. It was approaching 11.15pm when Stella reached the gravel turnout leading to the water pumping station. As she navigated the turn, her car's headlights swept across the area, illuminating a tan-colored
其余的子弹钻进她背部的右侧，导致她在离公路几步远的地方侧身倒下。随着两个年轻人倒下，袭击者逃跑了。他没有遇到斯特拉·博尔热斯，后者正开车沿着赫尔曼湖路去贝尼西亚的一家电影院接她的儿子。当斯特拉到达通往水泵站的砾石岔道时，时间已近晚上11点15分。当她拐弯时，她车的车灯扫过这片区域，照亮了一辆棕色的旅行车。

17
00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:51.000
station wagon. It sat alone in the dark, its passenger side door wide open. A young man was lying on the ground. Stella's stomach lurched. Then she saw the body of a young woman sprawled closer to the road. Too frightened to pull over, Stella sped onwards to Benesha. She turned down East Second Street and spotted a police cruiser in the distance. Desperate to get the officer's attention, Stella frantically honked her horn and flashed
它孤零零地停在黑暗中，副驾驶座的车门大开着。一个年轻男子躺在地上。斯特拉的胃里一阵翻江倒海。然后她看到了一个年轻女子的尸体倒在离公路更近的地方。由于太害怕而不敢停车，斯特拉加速向贝尼西亚开去。她拐进东第二街，看到远处有一辆警车。为了引起警官的注意，斯特拉拼命按喇叭并闪烁车灯。

18
00:11:51.000 --> 00:12:31.000
her headlights. The sight of Stella's discovery spread quickly, with police and paramedics converging at the turnout. As they approached the body of Betty Lou Jensen, it became clear she was deceased. Lying closer to the rambler was David Faraday. As officers moved in, they noticed a fleeting, misty cloud escape David's lips. He was still breathing. He was rushed to hospital, but died along the way.
斯特拉发现情况的消息迅速传开，警察和医护人员汇集到岔道。当他们靠近贝蒂·露·延森的尸体时，很明显她已经去世了。躺在离Rambler更近的是大卫·法拉第。当警官们走近时，他们注意到一团转瞬即逝的雾气从大卫的嘴里冒出来。他还在呼吸。他被紧急送往医院，但在途中死亡。

19
00:12:31.000 --> 00:13:09.000
Hours earlier, David Faraday had marched across the grounds of Hogan High School, where Betty Lou was an honour roll student. But David wasn't looking for Betty Lou. Witnesses watched as the typically mild-mannered David confronted 16-year-old Richard Burton. The pair exchanged some heated words, though they were discreet enough not to draw the attention of any nearby teachers. Fearful that he'd soon be spotted and get in trouble, David left before the altercation became physical.
几个小时前，大卫·法拉第曾穿过霍根高中的校园，贝蒂·露曾是那里的荣誉榜学生。但大卫不是来找贝蒂·露的。目击者看到通常温文尔雅的大卫与16岁的理查德·伯顿发生对质。两人交换了一些激烈的言辞，尽管他们足够谨慎，没有引起附近任何老师的注意。由于害怕很快被发现并惹上麻烦，大卫在冲突升级为肢体冲突之前离开了。

20
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:52.000
Word of this confrontation reached detectives investigating David's murder. They visited Hogan High, where they examined Betty Lou's locker. In her binder for English class, they found a note she had written. �Do you know a kid named Richard Burton?� it read. I was going with him until two days before the installation. He still phones me and is threatening me to keep away from Dave. He said that if he's ever close enough to Dave, he would punch him one in the teeth. I told him to leave me alone, if he knows what's good for him.
这场对质的消息传到了调查大卫谋杀案的侦探们耳中。他们走访了霍根高中，检查了贝蒂·露的储物柜。在她的英语课文件夹里，他们发现了一张她写的便条。“你认识一个叫理查德·伯顿的孩子吗？”上面写着，“我和他在一起，直到装置安装前两天。他还给我打电话，威胁我离大卫远点。他说如果他离大卫够近，他会狠狠揍他一顿。我告诉他离我远点，如果他知道什么对由他好的话。”

21
00:13:52.000 --> 00:14:36.000
Police were familiar with Richard Burton, who was also known as Ricky. He was currently on probation for stealing. An outsider with few friends, Ricky was often seen walking the school halls with Betty Lou and was rumoured to be pursuing a relationship with her. When Betty Lou started seeing David, Ricky was jealous. He'd been harassing her ever since, sometimes calling her house every 15 minutes. Betty Lou was convinced Ricky was spying on her and advised her sister and mother to keep the curtains closed at all times.
警方对理查德·伯顿很熟悉，他也叫里基。他目前正因盗窃处于缓刑期。里基是个没什么朋友的外来者，经常被看到和贝蒂·露一起走在学校走廊里，据传他一直在追求她。当贝蒂·露开始和戴维交往时，里基嫉妒了。此后他一直骚扰她，有时每15分钟就往她家打一次电话。贝蒂·露确信里基在监视她，并建议她的姐姐和母亲随时拉紧窗帘。

22
00:14:36.000 --> 00:15:18.000
On several occasions, they'd found the side gate to their house mysteriously open. Although they had no evidence to prove it, the Jensen family suspected Ricky might have been prowling around. The evening before she was killed, Betty Lou confided in her sister Melody that she was afraid of Ricky. He had threatened to tell Betty Lou's parents some of her secrets, such as the fact that she was a smoker and had started a relationship with David. Ricky had also threatened to beat David up using brass knuckles.
他们曾多次发现他们家的侧门莫名其妙地开着。尽管他们没有证据证明这一点，但延森一家怀疑里基可能一直在周围徘徊。在她被杀的前一天晚上，贝蒂·露向她的姐姐梅洛迪吐露心声，说她害怕里基。他曾威胁要把贝蒂·露的一些秘密告诉她的父母，比如她抽烟以及开始与大卫交往的事实。里基还威胁要用指节铜套殴打大卫。

23
00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:57.000
Melody advised Betty Lou to beat Ricky to it and tell their parents about David herself. Betty Lou followed her sister's advice and introduced her parents to David before they left for their date. When questioned, Ricky said the last time he'd spoken to Betty Lou was around 4.30pm on Thursday, December 19. He hadn't been at school that day, so he'd called her at home to see if there was anything he'd missed. He denied exchanging heated words with David on the day of the murders and insisted he'd
梅洛迪建议贝蒂·露抢先一步，自己把大卫的事告诉父母。贝蒂·露听从了姐姐的建议，在他们出门约会前将大卫介绍给父母。当被盘问时，里基说他最后一次和贝蒂·露说话是在12月19日星期四下午4点半左右。那天他没去学校，所以他给家里打电话看有没有落下什么。他否认在谋杀案当天与大卫交换过激烈的言辞，并坚称他

24
00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:35.000
never made any threats to David's face. Ricky was surprised but not upset to hear about the note Betty Lou had written about him. Ricky maintained he was home all night when David and Betty Lou were attacked. It was his sister's birthday and the family ate cake and watched a movie together until 11pm. Ricky said he went to bed at around 11.30 and learned of the shootings the following day. His parents confirmed he's alibi.
从未当面威胁过大卫。听到贝蒂·露写给他的便条，里基感到惊讶但并不沮丧。里基坚称在大卫和贝蒂·露遭到袭击时他一整夜都在家。那天是他姐姐的生日，一家人在一起吃蛋糕看电影直到晚上11点。里基说他在11点30分左右上床睡觉，第二天得知了枪击事件。他的父母证实了他的不在场证明。

